==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} {{initialism of|en|International Normalized Ratio}} An indicator of the [[clotting]] tendency of blood. Used, for example, to help determine dosage for patients during oral [[anticoagulant]] therapy. Outside the normal or target range, a high INR may indicate a higher risk of bleeding, while a low INR may suggest a higher risk of developing a clot.

